{
  "name": "vector_light_mask_max",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "\u00a727 phase 5: max(vanilla, ours) as the mask's LIFT, on the one scene where the two lighting models genuinely disagree about geometry \u2014 an open door. RimWorld's glow grid never learns a door opened, so beyond this one vanilla delivers nothing at all and \u00a727e's polygon looks straight through; the subtractive mask has no light there to keep, and the shipped composition answers with a flat additive beam at a strength somebody had to choose. Six arms from one midnight room and one torch: vanilla, the mask alone, the mask plus the shipped flat beam, THE CONTROL (phase 5's every line runs and delivers a lift of zero, which must reproduce the mask-alone frame exactly \u2014 it is what separates 'the max changed the frame' from 'relaxing two early-outs and clamping once instead of twice changed the frame'), the masked max itself, and the masked max with vanilla's intDist=100 seed dropped, which compares our curve at d against vanilla's at d+1 and so wins in every cell of every lamp rather than only where the geometry differs. Every arm states every \u00a727 flag; lift_samples and lift_peak are pinned as a pair because samples at 0 means the max never ran while peak at 0 over healthy samples means it ran and correctly found nothing, which is #151's finding rather than a failure.",
